			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help"><source>How filtering works</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.intro"><source>Pick one or more criteria to narrow the page tree down to the pages you are looking for.</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.combine"><source>Criteria from different categories are combined: a page has to match all of them. Picking several options within one category means any of them is enough.</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.chips"><source>Everything you picked is listed above. Remove a single criterion with its ×, or start over with "Reset".</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.scope"><source>"Search from current page down" limits the result to the page you currently have open and its subpages.</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.share"><source>"Copy link" copies a link to your current selection, so you can hand it to a colleague.</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.help.advanced"><source>Your selection also shows up as text in the page tree's search field. If you prefer typing, you can edit it there directly.</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.tabEmpty"><source>No options available</source></trans-unit>
			<trans-unit id="pagetreeFacets.modal.search"><source>Search filters</source></trans-unit>
